      "LIP-ET19-L3@5b4997e6dca27106533022b4ab46164cea073818"
    ],
    "productionEvidence": "PR #226 reports 63 candidate and 18 public checks without subject-bound ear anatomy comparison. PR #224 reports 39 candidate and 19 public checks, but its own visual review still records a hard inner-lip–gingiva transition. KX-20261013-01 notes that an anchor can be OBSERVED in one state/view and OCCLUDED or UNKNOWN in another.",
    "mechanism": "The N145 gate separated visible from occluded anchors but did not require a state×view matrix or bind each semantic anchor to its actual geometry/material carrier. Repeated screenshots from one state/view can therefore be mistaken for anatomy coverage, and hidden regions can receive invented measurements.",
